t:700;font-size:1.6em\">½</span> <span style=\"color:#5b6874;font-weight:700;font-size:0.9em\">= 0.5</span></div><ol class=\"rl\"><li><b class=\"rn\">1</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin 30° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">2</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos 60° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">3</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin 150° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">4</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos 300° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">5</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−cos 120° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">6</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−sin 210° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">7</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">45° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">8</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">45° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">9</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin 45° · cos 45° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">10</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">2 sin 15° cos 15° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">11</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">1 − sin 30° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">12</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">tan 30° · sin 60° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">13</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">1 / cosec 30° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">14</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">log</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>4</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> 2 = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">15</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">log</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>9</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> 3 = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">16</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">log</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>100</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> 10 = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">17</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">4</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>−½</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">18</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√0.25 = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">19</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">e</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>−ln 2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">20</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">Σ (½)</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>n</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">, n = 2 → ∞ = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">21</b><span>∫<sub>0</sub> <span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>1</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> x dx = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">22</b><span>∫<sub>0</sub> <span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>π/2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> sin x cos x dx = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">23</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">d/dx √x at x = 1 = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">24</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">lim(x→0) (1 − cos x)/x</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">25</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">lim(x→0) (√(1 + x) − 1)/x = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">26</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">average of sin</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">x over a cycle = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">27</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">η at maximum power transfer = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">28</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">pf at φ = 60° = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">29</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">pf when one wattmeter reads 0 = </span>½</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">30</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">P(head) for a fair coin = </span>½</span></li></ol><p style=\"color:#263238;font-size:1.10em\"><b>Remember:</b> Also: 0.693τ = time for a capacitor to fall to half. Maximum power transfer gives only 50% efficiency — half the power is lost in R_th. <span style=\"color:#ef6c00\"><b>Quick check:</b></span> sin 30° + cos 60°? <span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>Ans: ½ + ½ = 1</b></span></p><h4 style=\"font-size:1.46em;font-weight:700\">Everything that equals 1/√2 <span style=\"color:#5b6874\">— 30 expressions</span></h4><div class=\"rcv\" style=\"background:#ffffff;border-color:#15202b\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:1.6em\">0.707</span> <span style=\"color:#5b6874;font-weight:700;font-size:0.9em\">= 1/√2</span></div><ol class=\"rl\"><li><b class=\"rn\">1</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin 45° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">2</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos 45° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">3</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin 135° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">4</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos 315° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">5</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−cos 135° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">6</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−sin 225° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">7</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin(π/4) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">8</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos(π/4) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">9</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√2 / 2 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">10</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√0.5 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">11</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">2</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>−½</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">12</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sec 45° / 2 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">13</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cosec 45° / 2 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">14</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√(1 − sin</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">45°) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">15</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">(sin 45° + cos 45°)/2 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">16</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">2 sin 22.5° cos 22.5° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">17</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">22.5° − sin</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">22.5° = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">18</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">tan 45° / √2 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">19</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">Re(e</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>jπ/4</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">20</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">Im(e</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>jπ/4</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">21</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">|1 + j| / 2 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">22</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin 45° cos 45° √2 = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">23</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>rms</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">/V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>m</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> (sine) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">24</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">I</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>rms</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">/I</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>m</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> (sine) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">25</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>rms</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">/V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>m</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> (full-wave rectified) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">26</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">I / I</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>max</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> at half-power points = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">27</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">voltage ratio at −3 dB = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">28</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">pf when R = X (φ = 45°) = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">29</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">ζ of 2nd-order Butterworth = </span>1/√2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">30</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">Q of 2nd-order Butterworth = </span>1/√2</span></li></ol><p style=\"color:#263238;font-size:1.10em\"><b>Remember:</b> Half-power points: current is 0.707 of maximum, so power I²R is half. At ζ = 0.707 the overshoot is 4.3% with no resonant peak. <span style=\"color:#ef6c00\"><b>Quick check:</b></span> V_m = 100 V. RMS value of the sine? <span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>Ans: 70.7 V</b></span></p>",[]],"1429":["<h4 style=\"font-size:1.46em;font-weight:700\">Everything that equals √3 <span style=\"color:#5b6874\">— 30 expressions</span></h4><div class=\"rcv\" style=\"background:#ffffff;border-color:#15202b\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:1.6em\">1.732</span> <span style=\"color:#5b6874;font-weight:700;font-size:0.9em\">= √3</span></div><ol class=\"rl\"><li><b class=\"rn\">1</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">tan 60° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">2</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cot 30° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">3</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">tan 240° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">4</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cot 210° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">5</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−tan 120° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">6</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−tan 300° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">7</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">tan(π/3) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">8</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">2 sin 60° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">9</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">2 cos 30° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">10</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sin 60° / cos 60° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">11</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cos 30° / sin 30° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">12</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">1 / tan 30° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">13</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">3 tan 30° = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">14</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">3 / √3 = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">15</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√12 / 2 = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">16</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√(sec</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">60° − 1) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">17</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√(cosec</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">30° − 1) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">18</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">√(2</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> − 1</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">19</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cube diagonal ÷ side = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">20</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">equilateral △: height ÷ half-side = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">21</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>L</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">/V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>ph</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> in star = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">22</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">I</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>L</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">/I</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>ph</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> in delta = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">23</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">|V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>R</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> − V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>Y</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">| / |V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>R</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">| = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">24</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">factor in P = √3 V</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>L</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> I</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>L</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> cos φ = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">25</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">400 V ÷ 230 V (≈) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">26</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">11 kV ÷ 6.35 kV (≈) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">27</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">33 kV ÷ 19.05 kV (≈) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">28</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">factor in tan φ = √3 (W</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>1</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> − W</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>2</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">)/(W</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>1</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> + W</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sub>2</sub></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">) = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">29</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">tan φ when one wattmeter reads 0 = </span>√3</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">30</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">X/R when pf = 0.5 = </span>√3</span></li></ol><p style=\"color:#263238;font-size:1.10em\"><b>Remember:</b> Star: line VOLTAGE = √3 × phase. Delta: line CURRENT = √3 × phase. The √3 always goes with the line quantity. <span style=\"color:#ef6c00\"><b>Quick check:</b></span> Star, phase voltage 230 V. Line voltage? <span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>Ans: 230 × 1.732 = 398 ≈ 400 V</b></span></p><h4 style=\"color:#e65100;font-size:1.46em;font-weight:700\">Everything that equals 2 <span style=\"color:#5b6874\">— 30 expressions</span></h4><ol class=\"rl\"><li><b class=\"rn\">1</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sec 60° = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">2</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cosec 30° = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">3</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">sec</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">45° = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">4</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">cosec</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">45° = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">5</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−sec 120° = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">6</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">−cosec 210° = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">7</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">1 / sin 30° = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">16</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">∛8 = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">17</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">e</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>ln 2</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"> = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">18</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">|1 + j√3| = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">19</b><span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">Σ (½)</span><span style=\"color:#15202b\"><sup>n</sup></span><span style=\"color:#15202b\">, n = 0 → ∞ = </span>2</span></li><li><b class=\"rn\">20</b><span>∫<sub